rown-up","I want to be a grown-up.",null],["to be fun","This book is interesting.",null],["an ankle","I twisted my ankle on the stairs.",null],["underwear","Put the underwear in the drawer.",null],["a diary","I write in a diary every night.",null],["to burn","We burn the fallen leaves.",null],["a place, a venue","We decided the venue.",null],["Sunday","I rest on Sunday.",null],["a drawer","I put the key in the drawer.",null],["the sun","The sun is hot.",null],["oneself","Everyone does their own work.",null],["the head","I nodded my head.",null],["a function, a feature","This phone has a great many functions.",null],["broadcasting","The broadcast is starting.",null],["a glove","It's cold, so put on gloves.",null],["one's turn","It's my turn now.",null],["to be red","The apple is red.",null],["a coin","Please put a coin in.",null],["fog","The fog was thick this morning.",null],["noodles","I had noodles for lunch.",null],["slowly","I walk slowly.",null],["effort","Effort is needed.",null],["to be near","The school is near.",null],["the word used when counting flat sheets","I need three sheets of paper.",null],["being special","There is a special discount at the weekend.",null],["a wrist","I put a watch on my wrist.",null],["to be clear, to be fine","The sky is clear.",null],["Wednesday","I go to the hospital on Wednesday.",null],["a monthly salary","The salary came in yesterday.",null],["Thursday","Please wait until Thursday.",null],["the environment","We have to protect the environment.",null],["to be cold to the touch","The water is cold.",null],["a news article","I read the article.",null],["a kind or type","There are many kinds of fruit.",null],["a long time","I waited a long time.",null],["Monday","I start work on Monday.",null],["to be clean","The clothes are very clean.",null],["to come about, to appear","A new shop has appeared.",null],["a plant","I put a plant by the window.",null],["an onion","Cutting onions makes my eyes water.",null],["an occupation","What is your occupation?",null],["to be cold","It's cold today.","A ㅂ-irregular adjective: before a vowel the ㅂ becomes 우, so it is 추워요, 추웠어요 and 추운 날 (a cold day), while 춥고 and 춥습니다 keep the ㅂ. 덥다 (hot), 어렵다 (difficult), 쉽다 (easy) and 가깝다 (near) all work the same way. It is about the weather or the air; a cold drink is 차갑다."],["table","The table is wide.",null],["to take along","Please take an umbrella.",null],["by any chance","Do you have time, by any chance?",null],["to be, politely","Grandmother is in the room.",null],["air","The air is clean.",null],["a face mask","I put on a mask.",null],["a middle-aged woman","The lady gave me soup.","The everyday, blunt word for a woman of your parents' age. Said *to* her it often lands as an insult about her age. 아주머니 is the polite form, and 저기요 avoids the problem."],["a basement","I put the luggage in the basement.",null],["usually, ordinary","I usually get up at seven.",null],["space, the universe","The universe is very wide.",null],["email","I sent an email.",null],["a pillow","The pillow is soft.",null],["without","I came without money.",null],["of course","Of course it's fine.",null],["voice","You have a nice voice.",null],["to close, to shut","I close the door.",null],["to give to an elder","I give a gift to my teacher.",null],["a teacher","That person is a school teacher.","The plain form of the word for teacher. In practice Koreans nearly always say 선생님, with the honorific 님 — a teacher is addressed and referred to that way even by other adults. 선생 on its own can sound curt."],["to dig","I dig the ground.",null],["to chat","Please talk slowly.",null],["to teach","I teach Korean.",null],["church","I go to church on Sunday.",null],["to be quiet","The library is quiet.",null],["a dumpling","The dumplings are very tasty.",null],["Tuesday","There is a test on Tuesday.",null],["Chinese cabbage","We make kimchi with Chinese cabbage.",null],["a postcard","I sent a postcard from the trip.",null],["area","This area is quiet.",null