 person can be 밝다 in the sense of cheerful, or 밝다 about a subject, meaning well informed about it."],["documents, paperwork","I prepared the documents.",null],["reality","Reality is harder than expected.",null],["to be impressive","Your ability is impressive.",null],["high school","My younger sibling goes to high school.",null],["to be sleepy","I get sleepy after I eat.",null],["to come to visit","A friend came to visit.",null],["a.m.","I have class in the morning.",null],["laughter","I can't help laughing.",null],["thanks to someone's help","Thanks to a friend, I found the way.",null],["a hero","He is a hero.",null],["a hair","The hair is long.",null],["to come undone","My shoelace has come undone.",null],["to be low","The chair is low.",null],["to tie up, to bind","I tied up my hair.",null],["even so, still","It's raining. Even so, I'll go.",null],["orange","The orange is sweet.",null],["most, the majority","Most of them are students.",null],["the future","I think about the future.",null],["any, anyone","Come any time.",null],["the outside","It's cold outside.",null],["to dance","I dance.",null],["a queen","I saw an old queen's clothes at the museum.",null],["to be heavy","This box is heavy.",null],["after that","I haven't seen them since then.",null],["to shine","Your eyes are shining.",null],["a washing machine","I put the washing machine on.",null],["beggar","A beggar appears in the old tale.",null],["a half","I ate only half the bread.",null],["to move","Please don't move.",null],["really, truly","The weather is really lovely today.",null],["wine","I drink a glass of wine.",null],["a stage","I went up on stage.",null],["to step on, to tread on","I stepped on someone's foot.",null],["a cold","I caught a cold.",null],["six","Let's meet at six.",null],["the west","The sun sets in the west.",null],["success","I wish you success.",null],["excuse me","Excuse me.",null],["a wound","The wound hurts.",null],["a telephone number","What is your telephone number?",null],["a pocket, a pouch","I put it in my pocket.",null],["a week","I go twice a week.",null],["to get in touch","I'll get in touch when I arrive.",null],["cleaning","I clean the room.",null],["the word used when counting people","There are five students.","The counter for people, with native numbers: 학생 다섯 명 (five students), 두 명이요 (two, please — at a restaurant door). 몇 명이에요? asks how many people. 분 is the honorific counter for the same thing — 손님 두 분 — and 사람 can count informally too: 두 사람."],["happiness","I find happiness in small things.",null],["breath","I'm out of breath from coming up the stairs.",null],["to understand","I understood the explanation.",null],["an introduction","We met through a friend's introduction.",null],["arrival","The arrival was late.",null],["a star","That actor is a star.",null],["soldier","A soldier is standing there.",null],["a little while ago","I called a little while ago.",null],["to be dangerous","It's dangerous to go alone at night.",null],["to greet","I greeted my teacher.",null],["health","I walk every day for my health.",null],["a result","The result is good.",null],["to be sold","The tickets are all sold.",null],["to run","I run in the park.",null],["hard, diligently","I study hard.",null],["a piece of writing","I wrote a short piece.",null],["to lift","I lift the bag.",null],["to be hot","Summer is hot.","A ㅂ-irregular adjective, the pair of 춥다: 더워요, 더웠어요, 더운 날 before a vowel, 덥고 and 덥습니다 before a consonant. It describes weather, a room, or how you feel — 저는 더워요, I'm hot. Something hot to the touch, like food or water, is 뜨겁다 instead."],["to plant","I plant a tree.",null],["a receipt","May I have the receipt, please.",null],["monkey, ape","The monkey climbs the tree.",null],["motorcycle","The motorcycle is noisy.",null],["a date on the calendar","We set the date for the meeting.",null],["to follow","You have to follow the school rules.",null],["a check, confirmation","Please check.",null],["to be changed","The time has changed.",null],["to protect","They protect the country.",null],["to tie, to fasten","I tie my shoelaces.",null],["to hug, to hold in one's arms","I hold the baby.",null],["a trace","Traces were left on the snow.",null],["to remember","I still remember that person's name.",null],["the contents of something written or said","I read the contents of the letter again.",null],["to dislike","I don't like spicy food.",null],["to grow","The child is growing well.",null],["to be strange, to be unusual","The sound is strange.",null],["a cost","The repair cost a lot.",null],["someday","Someday I'll go to Korea.",null],["a woman of one's parents' age","I asked the lady for directions.","A woman of about your parents' age, and the more courteous of the two words for her — 아줌마 is the blunt one. Even so, 저기요 is the safe way to get a stranger's attention."],["the law","Everyone has to obey the law.",null],["a reservation","I moved the reservation to two o'clock.",null],["all day","It rained all day.",null],["cheers","Right, cheers!",null],["in a moment","I'll be right back.",null],["to be weak","The flame is weak.",null],["far away","I can see a mountain far away.",null],["a corridor","The corridor is quiet.",null],["to ask","I ask the teacher.",null],["knowledge","Knowledge comes from books.",null],["to be difficult, to be hard","This question is difficult.",null],["a museum","The museum is very big.",null],["an angel","There is an angel in the picture.",null],["to pick, to pluck","I picked an apple.",null],["to order food","I ordered pizza.",null],["to be safe","It is safe here.",null],["to return, to come back","I came back home.",null],["to gather","My friends gathered.",null],["a work of art","I saw a famous work at the art museum.",null],["soon","The meeting starts soon.",null],["three, before a counter","Three apples, please.",null],["to be surprised","I was startled by the noise.",null],["to play, to hang out","The children are playing.",null],["to get off","I get off at the next sta